// bubbler profile: firefox
//
// Sound is `pulseaudio`: Firefox is a libpulse client (`libpulse` is in
// the Arch package's Depends) and reaches the server through
// $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pulse/native, which is what that grant binds.
// `pipewire` binds only pipewire-0, the native socket, and is what the
// screen-share portal hands frames over. Either socket carries capture
// as well as playback: this is the microphone too.
//
// `network` is the sandbox's own network namespace. Chromecast discovery
// is mDNS on the LAN and pasta does not bridge, so casting does not find
// anything; `network "host"` brings it back, together with every service
// on the host's loopback.
//
// Gecko has defaulted to Wayland since Firefox 121 and takes the display
// from the `wayland` grant, so no `env` node sets MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND;
// `env MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND="0"` goes back to Xwayland.
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   pipewire
//     — screen and window sharing: the portal picks the source and hands
//       the stream over PipeWire, so both grants are needed.
//   dbus {
//       own "org.mozilla.firefox.*"
//   }
//     — in place of the bare `dbus` node above, since one config carries
//       one `dbus` node: the remote-instance protocol, which a second
//       `firefox` reaches the running one through instead of starting
//       beside it.
//   notify
//     — desktop notifications a page asks for. Needs `dbus`.
//   mpris name="firefox.*"
//     — media keys and the desktop's player controls for a tab that is
//       playing. Needs `dbus`.
//   app-runtime "org.keepassxc.KeePassXC"
//     — KeePassXC browser integration. Grant the same id in the
//       `keepassxc` instance (it lists the line in its own header).
//       Read-only is enough: this side only connects to the socket
//       KeePassXC serves.
wayland
dri
pulseaudio
network
dbus
portals
home-share "Downloads" mode=rw
command "firefox"
